1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,504
May every website of an approved merchant take payments?

2
00:00:03,554 --> 00:00:09,288
In Lesson 18, the merchant was switched on, and in Lesson 20, its team got their roles.

3
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:14,208
But a merchant may run several websites, and each one is a different risk.

4
00:00:14,258 --> 00:00:17,856
This lesson checks and switches on each website on its own.

5
00:00:17,906 --> 00:00:24,504
Picture a merchant with an approved company that adds a second website: a copy of a famous brand's shop.

6
00:00:24,554 --> 00:00:30,504
If every website could take payments the moment it was typed in, all the bank's checks on the company would mean nothing.

7
00:00:30,554 --> 00:00:35,232
A market licenses the company, but every stall is still inspected on its own.

8
00:00:35,282 --> 00:00:37,728
A merchant's websites work the same way.

9
00:00:37,778 --> 00:00:39,600
Here is how it works.

10
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:43,536
Each website is a sales point: one place where buyers pay.

11
00:00:43,586 --> 00:00:46,680
It starts as a draft, and a draft cannot take money.

12
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:50,040
When a payment ends, the buyer is sent back to the shop.

13
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:52,080
Where they go is a return address.

14
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:56,232
Every return address must be secure, and on the website's own site.

15
00:00:56,282 --> 00:01:00,744
So a payment can never send a buyer somewhere else, like a fake thank-you page.

16
00:01:00,794 --> 00:01:05,112
Return addresses can change only while the website is still a draft.

17
00:01:05,162 --> 00:01:11,088
Next, a bank admin checks the site, and records a site check: passed or failed.

18
00:01:11,138 --> 00:01:13,272
A failed check must say what is wrong.

19
00:01:13,322 --> 00:01:15,144
Then the deal.

20
00:01:15,194 --> 00:01:17,400
It says which cards the website takes.

21
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:20,784
It can also say how much it may take per payment, and per day.

22
00:01:20,834 --> 00:01:26,160
Only with an active merchant, a passed check and at least one card can the website be switched on.

23
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:30,912
Each card still needs its own terminal and its own fee before its payments go through.

24
00:01:30,962 --> 00:01:37,800
And before taking any money, every part of the system asks one question: may this website take a payment right now?

25
00:01:37,850 --> 00:01:42,024
The answer is yes only when the website and its merchant are both active.

26
00:01:42,074 --> 00:01:43,896
Now watch the product.

27
00:01:43,946 --> 00:01:47,856
The viewer signs in as the merchant and opens Websites.

28
00:01:47,906 --> 00:01:52,752
The page says each website that takes payments is checked and switched on by the bank.

29
00:01:52,802 --> 00:01:54,624
They click Add website.

30
00:01:54,674 --> 00:02:01,272
They give it a name, the website's address, and return addresses on that same site, pressing Enter after each one.

31
00:02:01,322 --> 00:02:04,080
Saved, the page says the bank will check it.

32
00:02:04,130 --> 00:02:07,392
Now the viewer tries a return address on somebody else's site.

33
00:02:07,442 --> 00:02:10,368
The server refuses it, and the screen shows why.

34
00:02:10,418 --> 00:02:12,552
Next, the bank admin portal.

35
00:02:12,602 --> 00:02:15,336
The admin opens the merchant and this website.

36
00:02:15,386 --> 00:02:20,880
A card at the top says "Before it takes payments", with a list of steps and how many are left.

37
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:22,824
The Switch on button is grey.

38
00:02:22,874 --> 00:02:28,488
A line explains: switching on needs an active merchant, a passed check and chosen cards.

39
00:02:28,538 --> 00:02:32,640
The admin clicks Record a check, chooses Passed, and saves.

40
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:34,512
Then Deal terms.

41
00:02:34,562 --> 00:02:36,384
They tick one card.

42
00:02:36,434 --> 00:02:41,832
The boxes "Most per payment" and "Most per day" can stay empty, which means no limit.

43
00:02:41,882 --> 00:02:45,576
Three steps now show done, and the Switch on button lights up.

44
00:02:45,626 --> 00:02:47,448
One click.

45
00:02:47,498 --> 00:02:54,120
A warning appears: some cards still have no terminal or fee, and their payments are refused until they do.

46
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:55,992
What does this protect?

47
00:02:56,042 --> 00:03:01,104
Without a check on each website, a copycat shop could ride on an approved company.

48
00:03:01,154 --> 00:03:07,800
Without strict return addresses, a fraudster could use the bank's own payment page to send buyers to a fake page.

49
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:10,704
The site check protects buyers and the bank's name.

50
00:03:10,754 --> 00:03:17,832
The single question asked before any money moves means a suspended website or merchant stops at once, everywhere.

51
00:03:17,882 --> 00:03:24,192
So, like a market stall: the company is licensed, and every website is still inspected on its own.

52
00:03:24,242 --> 00:03:27,144
Next: how the bank's fee is decided.
